# iOS Architecture

Before writing or editing anything under `iOSApp/`, read and follow `iOSApp/AGENT.md`.

## Layers (dependency goes downward only)

```
View → ViewModel → UseCase → Repository → DB/API
```

- **Presentation:** SwiftUI Views + ViewModels
- **Domain:** pure Swift models, repository protocols, use cases — no UIKit/SwiftUI/GRDB/Supabase
- **Data:** repository implementations, GRDB local models, remote clients

## Folder rules

- One ViewModel per View. Never share a ViewModel across Views.
- Feature folders import `Domain` and `Core` only — never another feature.
- Domain models never import GRDB, Supabase, or other frameworks.
- Wire new features in this order: Domain model → repo protocol → Data impl → UseCase → ViewModel → View → `AppContainer`.

## Hard bans (see AGENT.md §14)

- No business logic / API / DB calls in a View `body`
- No `SwiftUI` import in ViewModels
- No `.shared` singletons inside ViewModels or Use Cases — inject via `init`
- No raw LLM model strings — use `LLMClient.complete(tier:)`
- No hardcoded colors/fonts — use `Color.theme.*` / `Font.theme.*` (`docs/design/theme-guide.md`)
- No `NavigationView` — use `NavigationStack` + `AppRouter`
- No `DispatchQueue.main.async` — use `@MainActor`
- No force unwraps except documented `try!` in `DatabaseManager` migrations

When unsure, check the matching section in `iOSApp/AGENT.md` before implementing.

## After code changes — verify with xcodebuild

After any meaningful Swift/project change under `iOSApp/`, run a terminal build before considering the work done. Prefer the repo root as cwd. Pick **one** command based on the situation:

**1. Full Debug build (default)** — use after feature work, when you need a real signed Debug build, or when checking packaging/signing-related issues:

```bash
xcodebuild \
  -project iOSApp/MindMapper/MindMapper.xcodeproj \
  -scheme MindMapper \
  -configuration Debug \
  -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' \
  build
```

**2. Compile-only / type-check (faster)** — use for quick iteration, CI-style checks, or when codesigning would block (no team/profile). Prefer this for most mid-task verify loops:

```bash
xcodebuild \
  -project iOSApp/MindMapper/MindMapper.xcodeproj \
  -scheme MindMapper \
  -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' \
  build \
  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO
```

Fix any build errors before finishing. Do not skip this step after non-trivial iOS code changes.
